  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The square root of a negative number is not a real number, while the square root of a non-negative number is a real number.\n\nLet's look at each square root in turn.\n\n- $\\sqrt{-13}$ is the square root of $-13,$ which is a negative number. So $\\sqrt{-13}$ is not a real number.\n\n- $\\sqrt{29}$ is the square root of $29,$ which is a non-negative number. So $\\sqrt{29}$ is a real number.\n\n- $\\sqrt{-35}$ is the square root of $-35,$ which is a negative number. So $\\sqrt{-35}$ is not a real number.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\".",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
